---
import TextPage from '~/layouts/TextPage.astro';
import { PRODUCT_COUNT } from '~/data/products';
import { TOP_CATEGORIES } from '~/data/categories';
import { LOCATIONS } from '~/data/locations';
import { CONTACT, TEL_HREF, BUSINESS_PENDING } from '~/config/site';

const path = '/about/';
---

<TextPage
  title="About Cone Sleeves UK | Printed Packaging Supplier"
  description="Who we are, how we work, and the claims we deliberately do not make. A UK supplier of printed cone sleeves and food packaging."
  path={path}
  h1="About Cone Sleeves UK"
  standfirst="We print cone sleeves, food sleeves, trays, cups, papers and bags for food businesses across the United Kingdom, sized from the products they already serve."
  crumbLabel="About"
  pageType="AboutPage"
>
  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>
    We supply printed packaging to UK food businesses: ice cream shops, dessert bars,
    cafés, takeaways, bakeries, street food traders and event caterers. The catalogue runs
    to {PRODUCT_COUNT} products across {TOP_CATEGORIES.length} ranges, and every one of them is quoted against a
    specification rather than sold from a shelf.
  </p>
  <p>
    The common thread is that nothing is a stock size. A cone sleeve is cut to the cone you
    already buy, a cup sleeve to the cup already in your cupboard, a tray to the portion
    you already serve. That is the part most packaging orders get wrong, so it is where we
    start.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    Send us the product — a cone, a cup, a container, or a photograph of a made-up
    portion with a ruler beside it. We cut the die from that, confirm the board, lining,
    print method and finish in writing, and send a flat sample where the job allows it
    before anything is printed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Artwork goes onto a template shaped to your product, which we supply before design
    work begins. Our <a href="/artwork-guidelines/">artwork guidelines</a> set out the file
    formats, bleed and colour information we need.
  </p>

  <h2>What we will not do</h2>
  <p>
    A great deal of packaging marketing consists of numbers that apply to nothing in
    particular. We have deliberately left those off this website.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No published lead times.</strong> Turnaround moves with the print method, the
      run length and how busy the press is that month. Yours goes on your quote.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No single minimum order quantity.</strong> It follows from the print method
      your job needs, and a short digital run behaves nothing like a long conventional one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No blanket recycling claims.</strong> We tell you exactly what board, lining
      and finish a quoted item uses. Whether it is recycled depends on the collection
      available where it is thrown away, which we do not control.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No reviews, ratings or testimonials.</strong> None have been independently
      collected, so none are published. You will not find star ratings in our page markup
      either.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No claims of local offices.</strong> Our <a href="/locations/">area pages</a>
      describe the trade in each place, not branches we do not have.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where we supply</h2>
  <p>
    Anywhere in the United Kingdom. Orders travel on national carriers, and we cover
    {LOCATIONS.length} areas in detail on this site because there is something specific worth saying about
    the trade in each. Delivery to everywhere else works exactly the same way — see
    <a href="/delivery-information/">delivery information</a> for how dates are given.
  </p>

  <h2>Talking to us</h2>
  <p>
    We work by email and telephone and post physical samples rather than meeting in person.
    Sizing questions are almost always quicker on the phone with the product in your hand.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Telephone and WhatsApp: <a href={TEL_HREF}>{CONTACT.phoneDisplay}</a></li>
    <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a></li>
  </ul>

  {
    !BUSINESS_PENDING.legalName && (
      <p class="pending">
        <strong>Business details pending confirmation</strong>
        Registered company name, company registration number, VAT number and registered
        address have not been published because they have not yet been supplied for this
        site. They are configured through environment variables and will appear in the
        footer and in the page markup as soon as the real values are provided. Nothing has
        been invented in their place.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>Start an enquiry</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us what you serve and roughly how many you need, and we will come back with a
    specification you can actually compare against another quote.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/request-a-quote/">Request a quote</a>
  </p>
</TextPage>
